## SEVERITY / VERDICT (the grading rule is decided HERE; apply it, do not re-argue it)
*Blocker:* a path beyond the four; a commit count other than 3; a product, workflow, package, lock or csproj byte; a head blob other than the four named; a removed line beyond the 25 accounted; a non-ASCII byte, a person's name, a decision-card id, a `B###` token or a ticket key in an added line or any commit message; a skip, sleep, retry, environment or provider gate, a port literal, a new file access other than the one `readFileSync`; an existing test body or name changed beyond the three slice sites and the reason lines; **a loosening: the text a runner row judges differs between base and head on the real script (Check 4a), or the scanner deletes real code of `e2e.mjs`**; any existing test red at the head, the web suite not base + 17 or the Api class not base + 12, names lost above 0 or added other than the 17 and 12; **a new cell or row red, not `Passed`, skipped or missing on any run of Check 2 or on the SQL Server shard (Check 6)**; **`--check-shards` not rc 0 at the head or with current main's `ci.yml` (`e63d2966`) in place, or the real `ciMatrix` returning other than the five shard names**; the head moved; a red or cancelled check-run; a CodeQL alert open on the head (either threshold), a missing analysis at the verdict, or an alert dismissed other than by the org; a textual conflict in Check 8; a secret.
*Major, class SAME (the class is "held-name cells, runner source-text rows and the `ciMatrix` regex, tests and tooling only"):* **(M1) a cell or row that cannot fail:** a mutant of X-plain-2..5 (any distribution or single), S900/S933/S498 against the head rows (must stay 0 red: a RED there is a false red), the inverted helper, or a `ciMatrix` pattern mutant that leaves its named row(s) green, not shown equivalent by a run; **(M2) a pin that turns an equivalent or legitimate maintainer edit red** (Check 4d), or a code-reading row left raw, or a comment-text row read through the remover (Check 5); **(M3) `ciMatrix` accepts what it must refuse or refuses what it must accept** (a `#` with no blank before it accepted, a second line guessed, a trailing blank or `# note` refused) or the pattern is not linear (Check 4c); **(M4) a doc or reason sentence the repository contradicts** (Check 1).
*Major, class DIFFERENT:* a builder claim contradicted by measurement with a verdict consequence (the 17 web / 12 Api new names, 2955 / 108, the 16-of-16 and 42-of-42 kill counts, S498 = 2, the 0 / 9 legitimate-edit run, the census 3 + 5 -> 0 + 5): if your figures contradict the builder's the verdict carries the contradiction.
*Minor / Note (never a Major):* X-plain-6 and X-plain-mirror surviving (the named boundaries of item 2, a candidate decision for Tuesday); CRLF text returning `[]` at both sides (information, `ci.yml` has no carriage returns); `slice(at + 1)` -> `slice(at)` equivalent; a guard no mutant reaches; the n = 2 cells beyond the commission (accepted by the survivor measured at base); the SQL Server `databases` figure differing from main's 281; web test names not listed in the vitest log; 10 repeats instead of 20; the PR title's ticket key (the squash message is Tuesday's); the unsigned commits; the whole Api project not run on SQLite; GitHub's runner timing; bash/python/node/dotnet minor version differences from the runner.
*Where the line between Note and Major is unclear:* a thing that makes a cell or row unable to fail, or turns a legitimate edit red, is at least Major SAME; a thing that changes only what a message or a comment says and stays true is a Note. Say which rule you applied for every finding.
**VERDICT RULES.** GO needs Checks 1 to 9 clean and measured, both CodeQL thresholds met on a COMPLETE scan (4 of 4 analyses at `e7c2476`, 0 open alerts), every check-run `completed` `success` (the CodeQL umbrella, both SQL Server shards and the aggregator included), the 12 new names read `Passed` in the SQL Server shard's results, 0 findings above Note. **While any check-run of the head is pending the verdict is at most GO WITH FINDINGS and its text carries `(conditional: CI pending: <names>)`, never a bare GO; while the SQL Server shards are pending add `SQL Server rows not yet read`.** GO WITH FINDINGS = Minor/Note only. NO GO on any Blocker or Major; this is round 1 of 2, so a NO GO here does NOT reach the round cap: STATUS gives each Major's mutant (diff against the head file), the red set by name (or "none: green"), your run's output and a fix-shape in prose. NOT GATED = the head moved, the PR is not open, or a moved guarded region. A security-shaped finding is a STOP for tier 1.
**VERDICT LINES (one place, binding).** **First line of STATUS (placeholder at Step 0: `GATE VERDICT B693: PENDING`; verdict form, one line):** `GATE VERDICT B693: #220 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> @ e7c2476 (round 1 of 2 on class "held-name cells, runner source-text rows and the ciMatrix regex, tests and tooling only" - delta <3 commits, 4 paths, +151 -25 by program y/n; head blobs y/n; removed lines 25 accounted y/n; added lines placed y/n; product/workflow/package files 0 y/n; hygiene y/n; non-ASCII 0 y/n> - no-loosening <3 cuts equal y/n; scanner vs independent equal y/n> - names <web base -> head files/tests, lost n added n (17); Api class 96 -> 108 lost n added n (12); duplicates 0 y/n> - suites <web lint rc n, typecheck rc n, check-shards rc n; 10 repeats per pool red n; Api class SQLite n/n/n> - cells <X-plain-2..5 any and single: n built, red as predicted n, survivors <names|none>; base rows 0 red y/n; boundaries X-plain-6 and mirror survive y/n; c0 y/n; cw-weak y/n; c-fail y/n> - runner <S900/S933/S498 base rows red n/n/n, head rows red 0 y/n; inverted helper red y/n; pattern mutants n red of n; legitimate edits red n of n; pattern linear y/n; real ciMatrix five names at the base's and at current main's ci.yml y/n> - census <before 3+5, after 0+5 y/n; reason lines true y/n> - SQL Server <aggregator + 2 shards completed success y/n; 12 new names Passed y/n; trx read y/n; outcomes n (main 1150); databases n floor 100> - CI <n completed success of n; pending <names|none>; CodeQL umbrella <conclusion>; vitest n/n; Api.Tests n (main 1991)> - CodeQL <analyses n of 4 at the head; open alerts n; dismissed n> - merge <mergeable_state; merge-tree vs main <sha7> rc n; tree equals GitHub's y/n; lanes #219 and main's e63d2966 shared 0 y/n; main still e63d2966 y/n> - Jira <HPSMPOC-352 clause 1 met / clause 2 not met; HPSMPOC-349 stays open y/n> - gitleaks rc <n>)`. Then the sections: Step 0 (sha256s, slot count), REFUSE counts, PINS (start and verdict), instrument and load, Checks 1-9 each with the FAIL clock and evidence path, findings `B693-n` (severity, class SAME or DIFFERENT for a Major with the rule applied, `path:line` at the head, instrument, FAIL met, mutant diff, fix-shape in prose, evidence class MEASURED AT RUNTIME / PROBED / READ ONLY; "none" is valid), the cell kill table (mutant x new cell, base and head), the runner/ciMatrix table (mutant x row x base x head), the probe table, the census table, the SQL Server row table (shard, name, outcome, duration), the CI-job table (job, covers for this PR, does not cover), FOR TUESDAY (the verdict in plain words; whether the head-pinned squash can go now and the exact command; what CI still owes while checks are pending, naming the SQL Server shards; that this is round 1 of 2; the open residue as candidate decisions: item 2 of the ticket (six or more extra spaces, the mirrored split), reflow tolerance, the CRLF note, the ticket moves, the squash wording), FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections / processes, ports and trees left, **UNMEASURED** (at least: the floor-style SQL Server behaviour of trailing-space cells if the artifact was unreadable; GitHub's runner timing; the mutants and probes you cut). **Last line of STATUS: ONE line, exactly one of:** `VERDICT: B693 pr220 b683/hpsmpoc-e2e-runner-rows @ e7c2476 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> (round 1 of 2<; conditional: CI pending: names, only when it is>; CI <complete|pending: names|red: names>; SQL Server rows <read Passed|NOT READ|red>) on main <sha7>` (main by `ls-remote` at verdict), with the findings ids, severities and classes in the line above it (`B693-1 Note`), or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`.

**STATUS-NOW (binding).** **Write the STATUS file at Step 0 and keep it updated; a STATUS that does not exist while your logs move is a failure of this brief.** At Step 0, before any heavy work, write `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/!CODING/Datasec/HPSM-POC/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-10-25_B693_STATUS.md` holding: the placeholder FIRST line `GATE VERDICT B693: PENDING`; Step 0 (sha256s of the brief and its copy, the slot count with its control, your Step-0 date with the target verdict and HARD STOP written absolute); the REFUSE counts; PINS (the head, main, `compare` ahead/behind, the open-PR list, `mergeable_state`, check-run counts and CodeQL analysis count at your start); and one line per check (1-9) saying done / running / not started, with the evidence path of what is done. Update it after every check and every mutant batch. Do NOT write a `VERDICT:`, `STOPPED:` or `READY` line at the end until you mean it (a watcher fires on those). Evidence goes in `Briefs/2026-10-25_B693_evidence/` (summaries, hashes, TSVs, test-output excerpts, CI extracts; no secrets, no scripts, no person's name). Also write `## PROGRESS and RESUME` at about 80% of your context or at the hard stop (per step done/partial/not started, next exact commands, every scratch mutant with its restore proof), stop every process of yours, release the lock, and end the FILE with `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY continue in a fresh seat from RESUME?`.
